// Regression case for commit fc46e9db: an empty `\u{}` escape must be a parse
// error. Cedar rejects `"\u{}"` with `the input \u{} is not a valid escape`.
//
// The pre-fix decode_string parsed the braced body with
// `u32::from_str_radix("", 16)`, which fails on the empty string, so the code
// fell into its "malformed — pass through" branch and emitted `\`, `u`, `{`,
// `}` verbatim — accepted and validated cleanly instead of rejected.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document == "\u{}" };
